# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF, also on Windows with core.autocrlf.
# The catalog files have a normal form with LF line ends (CatalogReader.WriteItem), and a
# conversion on checkout would change bytes that are signed and compared.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Signed files are bytes, not text: git must store and check them out exactly as they were
# signed, or the signature fails. keys.json is written in LF before it is signed.
keys/keys.json -text
*.sig -text
